      }
    ],
    "rulings": [
      {
        "answer": "It means that the condition for \"if your opponent has 4 or less memory\" is fulfilled when the memory is at 1 through 10 on your side, 0, or 1 through 4 on your opponent's side at the timing when this effect activates.  Similarly, the condition for \"if they have 4 or more\" is fulfilled when the memory is at 4 through 10 on your opponent's side at the timing when this effect activates.",
        "question": "What do this card's \"if your opponent has 4 or less memory\" and \"if they have 4 or more\" mean, exactly?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      },
      {
        "answer": "Yes, that's correct.",
        "question": "If my opponent has 4 memory when this effect activates, do both the effect where 1 of my opponent's Digimon with 8000 DP or more can't attack until the end of their turn and the effect where I delete 1 of their Digimon with 6000 DP or less activate?",
        "reference": "[1]"
      }
    ]
